            <ArticleTitle>Single coronary artery from the left sinus with atherosclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>163-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of a single coronary artery originating from the left sinus of Valsalva with extensive atherosclerosis in a patient presenting with unstable angina. The distal circumflex artery continued the course of the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
